  "note": "Election of 12 members for the two wards of Warrenpoint Urban District on 21 May 1958: East Ward 5 seats, West Ward 7. The council was Labour 6, Unionist 5 and Independent 1, a Labour gain from Independent.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Newry Telegraph, 24 May 1958, p. 4 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the six defeated candidates were added with their votes (Havern, Progressive, 164; Derek McKinley 161; Hourican 148; William McKinley 142; Barry, Irish Labour, 118; Murphy 112), forenames from the nominations printed in the same report, and the register (519), total poll (395) and spoilt papers (9) recorded. Corrected from the page image of Newry Telegraph, 24 May 1958, p. 4 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the six Labour candidates (McGreevy, Fay, Daly, McKevitt, O'Neill, Finnison) are printed there 'McGREEVY (Irish Labour)' and '(I.L.)', and Mr. Fay spoke 'on behalf of the Irish Labour Party'; Party_Name NI Labour -> Irish Labour and Party_As_Printed set to the Newry Telegraph's label (the Irish News, 23 May 1958, p. 1 prints 'Lab.', kept in Name_As_Printed)."
